# Secrets — never commit real credentials
.env

# Build output — Netlify builds this itself from source on every deploy, so it normally
# doesn't need to be committed at all.
#
# EXCEPTION: dist/v*/ — versioned release folders (see webpack.config.js). These DO get
# committed, on purpose, once a release is confirmed working — that's what makes an
# already-approved Partner Center manifest keep resolving correctly after future deploys,
# since Netlify's build is a clean checkout every time and won't otherwise preserve them.
#
# WARNING before committing any dist/v*/ folder: unlike legacy-root/taskpane.js (which has
# its real OPENROUTER_KEY redacted to a placeholder, re-injected at build time — see
# RestoreLegacyRootPlugin), a normal dist/v*/ build goes through webpack's DefinePlugin
# directly and WILL contain the real key in plain text. Redact it the same way before
# committing, or you'll put the live production key into git history.
dist/*
!dist/v*/

# Dependencies — regenerate with `npm install`
node_modules/
